      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-354907\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">4.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/2555#4541\">Computing a Unit Price With Conversion to Smaller Units</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"354907\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Purchasing homemade lemonade costs <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"28\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c24\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">$</mi><mn>36</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> per gallon. What's the unit price per cup?</p>\n<p>Assume that there are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"29\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> cups in one gallon.</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 5:37 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:55</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>"
