      "dom_id": "question-354914",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Sarah bought $1$ ounce of almonds and paid $$0.75$ for it. What's the unit price per pound?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ ounces in one pound.",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that there are $16$ ounces in each pound.  \n\nSince the price is $$0.75$ per ounce, to find the price per pound, we multiply by $16:$\n\n$$\n0.75\\times 16=12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the almonds cost $$12$ per pound.",
